{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgac93Fi2wJjGmYXfsf1y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `times_eq_mul` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem times_eq_mul (n m : Nat) : times n m = n * m := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => simp [times]\n  | succ k ih => simp [times, ih, Nat.succ_mul]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `n`:\n- **Base case:** `times 0 m` is `0` by definition, which equals `0 * m`.\n- **Step:** `times (k+1) m` unfolds to `times k m + m`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `k * m + m`, and `Nat.succ_mul` shows this equals `(k+1) * m`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":8268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":250,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26de6f79-3ea1-4037-979b-5db3d0530bb1","uuid":"93af85e7-914e-4eb1-abce-d53a25d7c478","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:10:19.281Z","request_id":"req_011Cgac932Z5HCzqujbfuzcu"}
